        {
          "file": "tests/acceptance/native.cjs",
          "line": 183,
          "issue": "The native dash assertion checks only that the HUD text is nonempty; it would also accept 'Dash ready' if dash input stopped working.",
          "evidence/reproduction": "Lines 176\u2013183 dispatch dash input but assert only dash.trim().length > 0. Strengthen this to require 'Dash spent' and observable horizontal displacement. This is a regression-test weakness, not an observed gameplay failure: the existing source, dist and offline touch reports each record 'Dash spent'."
        }
      ],
      "reason": "No release-blocking player, correctness or security issue found in the approved scope. Reviewed the normative documents, all eight runtime files, delivery helpers, boundary/archive tests, independent acceptance code, final-gate evidence and every referenced raw log. HEAD is de7e75fb88912b0cbca7ac4e5d66e72c92a7bf3c; runtime and recorded behavior hashes match the gate, and final status/staged/unstaged checks are clean. Independently ran 25 nonmutating unit tests, all passing, plus source checks, source/dist byte comparisons and ZIP integrity testing. Artifact hashes match the parent attestation. The parent's full 48-unit/16-browser gate, zero-vulnerability audit, independent nine-letter/three-exit campaigns, lifecycle variants and measured audio checks were reviewed, not rerun. No files were edited or artifacts regenerated. Public publication and actual model/session/fingerprint attestations remain separate parent gates; this verdict does not certify physical phones, other browsers or human accessibility/audio experience."
    }
